// Materialized as go.mod — see MaterializeCanaryFixture's .canary rule.
//
// Deliberately dependency-free. A canary with real requirements would make
// `aegis security verify-image` need network access and a working module proxy
// to say anything at all about gosec, which would turn a provisioning gate into
// a flake. What this fixture has to establish is narrower and is the thing that
// was actually broken: that gosec in the image has a Go toolchain, loads
// packages, and reports what it finds instead of exiting clean on nothing.
//
// The other half of P55.8 — that the module cache gets warmed at all — is not
// asserted here but by warmGoModuleCache treating a failed warm phase as fatal.
module aegis.canary/gosec

go 1.21
